      "ruleId": "ssc-ffa9699e-29d1-e8a9-e358-c2b99a2e54d3",
      "title": "Uncontrolled Resource Consumption in com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind",
      "description": "Affected versions of com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind are vulnerable to Deserialization of Untrusted Data / Uncontrolled Resource Consumption. In FasterXML jackson-databind versions before 2.12.7.1 and 2.13.x before 2.13.4, enabling the `UNWRAP_SINGLE_VALUE_ARRAYS` feature allows a specially crafted deeply nested array to exhaust system resources during deserialization. This can lead to application crashes or Denial of Service (DoS), as unvalidated input can exploit the lack of checks in the deserialization process.",
